{
  "title": "A Mighty Fortress Is Our God",
  "author": "Martin Luther (1483-1546); tr. Frederick H. Hedge (1805-1890)",
  "key": "C",
  "public_domain": true,
  "arrangement": [
    "Verse 1",
    "Verse 2",
    "Verse 3",
    "Verse 4"
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "label": "Verse 1",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "1",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "A mighty fortress is our God, a bulwark never failing;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 2,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 18,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 25,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 32,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 46,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 50,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Our helper He amid the flood of mortal ills prevailing.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 15,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 23,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 32,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 47,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 51,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For still our ancient foe doth seek to work us woe;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 31,
              "text": "Am"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "His craft and power are great, and armed with cruel hate,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 35,
              "text": "G"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "On earth is not His equal.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 3,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 12,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 16,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 20,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 2",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "2",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Did we in our own strength confide, our striving would be losing;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 18,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 30,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 40,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 58,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 61,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Were not the right Man on our side, the Man of God’s own choosing.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 5,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 23,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 30,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 40,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 57,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 62,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dost ask who that may be? Christ Jesus, it is He;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 5,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 33,
              "text": "Am"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Lord Sabaoth, His name, from age to age the same,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 5,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 29,
              "text": "G"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And He must win the battle.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 12,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 20,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 23,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 3",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "3",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "And though this world, with devils filled, should threaten to undo us,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 28,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 35,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 50,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 64,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 67,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "We will not fear, for God hath willed His truth to triumph through us.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 3,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 31,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 42,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 59,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 67,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Prince of Darkness grim, we tremble not for him;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 32,
              "text": "Am"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "His rage we can endure, for lo, his doom is sure,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 28,
              "text": "G"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "One little word shall fell him.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 11,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 27,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 4",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "4",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "That word above all earthly powers, no thanks to them, abideth;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 5,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 20,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 28,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 39,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 56,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 59,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The Spirit and the gifts are ours through Him who with us sideth.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 19,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 29,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 42,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 58,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 61,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Let goods and kindred go, this mortal life also;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 31,
              "text": "Am"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The body they may kill: God’s truth abideth still,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 30,
              "text": "G"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "His kingdom is forever.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 4,
              "text": "Am"
            },
            {
              "position": 12,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 18,
              "text": "G"
            },
            {
              "position": 20,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
